						<h6 class="uabb-adv-accordion-button-label" >What is pro rata invoicing and how does it work?</h6>
			<div class="uabb-adv-accordion-icon-wrap" ><i class="uabb-adv-accordion-button-icon fas fa-chevron-down"></i></div>		</div>
		<div class="uabb-adv-accordion-content uabb-adv-accordion-contentkj8wh1updox9 fl-clearfix uabb-accordion-desc uabb-text-editor" aria-expanded="true" >
			<p>Pro rata invoicing is our billing method based on the commencement date of your Ad On Workforce staff member/s. It applies when your staff member/s start/s on a day other than the first day of the month. The first invoice for the Staffing Fee and any Add-on Services will cover the period from the staff member's commencement date to the end of that month. However, if the staff member commences within 5 days of the end of the month, the first invoice will cover the commencement date to the end of the following month. This approach ensures that we don't send small invoices for a few days of fees and instead combines a full month's charges along with the days worked in the commencement month.</p>
